          "check": "clinical_scope_and_decisive_support",
          "result": "clear",
          "finding": "Diffuse nonradicular axial pain, nonspecific mild multilevel MRI degeneration and no established procedure target do not establish clinical necessity for immediate intradiscal PRP. The retained ASIPP 2025 recommendation expressly requires thorough diagnostic evaluation first; a moderate consensus recommendation does not remove that requirement. A separate low-back-pain guideline supports identifying chronicity risk and providing intensive multidisciplinary management if necessary. Functional decline, fear of movement and activity withdrawal make that second component relevant to this patient.",
          "source_ids": [
            "41481869",
            "34051387"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "population_safety_and_evidence_limits",
          "result": "clear",
          "finding": "The entry concerns an adult elective pain-clinic decision with intact neurologic findings and no reported red flags. It asks for diagnostic assessment without prescribing an unsupported diagnostic procedure, drug, biologic dose or automatic rejection of later PRP. Candidate B and the key explicitly permit later regenerative therapy alone or with other modalities and do not require failure or completion of a comprehensive multimodal program. The ASIPP evidence is fair Level III with scarce high-quality research; its consensus rating is not proof of treatment necessity for this patient.",
          "source_ids": [
            "41481869",
            "34051387"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "literal_passage_entailment",
          "result": "clear",
          "finding": "ASIPP passage p4 directly establishes diagnostic necessity, patient preferences, expectations, risks, costs and standalone or adjunctive use; p3 establishes Level III/fair intradiscal PRP evidence, with p4 supplying the research-quality limitation. The additional p5 chosen by one reviewer is consistent. The separate guideline p1 directly supports chronicity-risk identification and multidisciplinary care when necessary. All 13 quote instances are exact handle expansions.",
          "source_ids": [
            "41481869",
            "34051387"
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "reviewer_reasoning_limit",
          "result": "clear",
          "finding": "The blinded solver prose loosely suggests rehabilitation should precede any biologic procedure. This is not treated as evidence for a mandatory treatment sequence. The independently assessed authored answer, private key and final claim reviews expressly allow standalone later use and make diagnostic necessity the prerequisite. That distinction preserves the actual ASIPP statement."
        },
        {
          "check": "public_answer_cues",
          "result": "clear",
          "finding": "The title, question, consultation and descriptive MRI impression stop at the management decision. The patient request for an injection supplies the clinical choice, without instructing the applicant to accept or defer it. The private answer and grading fields are absent from the reconstructed public payload."
        },
